    "title": "Strauss, Mozart & Others Will Delight All in LCSA Fall Concert - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By The Bloom Curation Staff ,\n1 days ago The Lake County Symphony will present its 2025 Fall Concert on November 23 at 2 p.m. at the Soper Reese Theatre in Lakeport. Musical Director/Conductor John Parkinson opens the performance with the rousing “Radetsky March” by Austrian composer Johann Strauss Sr. (1804-1849). The piece is considered Strauss’s most famous. It was written to commemorate Field Marshal Joseph Radetzky von Radetz’s victory at the Battle of Custoza. Along with the “Blue Danube” waltz by his son, Johann Strauss Jr., who was known as the “Waltz King,” the march became an unofficial Austrian national anthem. It became very popular among regimented marching soldiers, who spontaneously clapped and stamped their feet when they first heard the chorus. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
